            <p>
                Small brewpubs who prefer to sell their packaged product at the source instead of distributing have a
                unique
                opportunity to be experimental with their labeling. When you distribute your product, having a
                consistent
                brand design helps consumers easily identify your brand on the crowded shelf. But if your consumers are
                already in your establishment, and you don’t have to compete for shelf space, go fucking wild!
                <br><br>
                The creativity within the craft beer industry goes hand in hand with illustrative design or
                collaborating
                with artists. Your beer label should be as unique as your beers. Unique labels easily translate into
                unique
                merchandising. The majority of these labels were created for Arizona Wilderness Brewing Co., based out
                of the Phoenix
                Arizona valley, but I’m always interested in working with new breweries who are not afraid to be
                <strong>bold!</strong>
            </p>
